<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Netherlands New Guinea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1949">1949</a>–<a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> was the western half of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a>, which the Netherlands kept when it transferred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the rest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">East Indies</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> in 1949. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> prepared it for separate self-government, but Indonesian military pressure and American mediation led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Agreement of 1962. The territory passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> administration that year and to Indonesia in 1963.</p></div>
